  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Test Description :</strong></span></p>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Antibodies against GAD are found in the serum and CSF of 60 % - 100% of patients with stiff-person syndrome(a rare neurological disease with progressive muscle frigidity , spasms and resulting skeletal deformations.) or its clinical variants (Stiff Limb Syndrome ;&nbsp;progressive encephalomyelitis with rigidity and myoclonia) GAD specific antibodies can also occur in cases of non paraneoplastic&nbsp;limbic encephalitis or cerbellar ataxia.</span></div>",
